 1. **Unified Conceptual Exit Boundary Plane:** The conceptual exit boundary of the hazard corridor is defined as the **Level-Crossing Departure Roadway Boundary Plane**—the transverse plane where the road and pedestrian corridor terminates on the departure side of the tracks. The "vendor-stall clearance line" and "departure roadway boundary" are **two descriptive names for this exact same physical exit boundary plane** (stationary vendor stalls line the departure roadway edge). This rule is an operational annotation convention, not an independently surveyed physical geodetic ground truth.
