 5. **$T_4$ (Tail Clearance):** Rear buffer of final rail vehicle clears the unified departure roadway exit boundary plane (vendor-stall clearance line observed on `camera_back.mov`), permitting pedestrian and vehicle ingress.
 6. **$T_{\text{scene\_clear}}$ (Scene Clear):** Train recedes completely past visible corridor sightlines under the viaduct on `camera_back.mov`. If recording ends while train is still visible, marked `unobservable: true, value_s: null`.
 7. **Left/Right-Censored Stream Handling:** Streams must be evaluated independently without cross-stream assumptions. If an arrival occurs pre-recording (e.g. `event_005` front camera), $T_1$ and $T_2$ are unobservable/left-censored. If a recording ends mid-passage (e.g. `event_005` back camera), $T_4$ is unobservable/right-censored.
+8. **Crossing conflict area (CCA).** The stretch of railway alignment within the road-and-pedestrian crossing corridor, bounded along the direction of travel by an **entry boundary** (landmark DEFERRED, RD-006) and the **exit plane** (Level-Crossing Departure Roadway Boundary Plane, marked by the vendor-stall clearance line on `camera_back.mov`). The train occupies the CCA while any part of any rail vehicle lies between them. No coordinates, distances or survey are implied.
