+### 5.5 Camera Roles and Independent-Camera Analysis (RD-015, RD-028)
+
+- **Independent-camera analysis is primary.** Front-camera-dependent metrics (Missed-Train with lead-in screen, Warning Lead Time) use the **front-stream replay**; $T_4$-dependent metrics (M4, M5) use the **back-stream replay**. Front and back outputs are reported separately and never merged into one score.
+- **Fused (R04) analysis is exploratory only.** R04 remains unresolved; the authorized exploratory scope is the existing 11-event set; no official dual-camera scope exists. The unmet 20/23 calibration requirement is not satisfied and is not claimed. Acoustic synchronization offsets never shift human ground-truth timestamps (RD-027); they may support only explicitly authorized replay fusion.
+- A back-stream M5 is *replay-relative*: "never protected by that replay's sensing".
+
+### 5.6 Metric Scope and Status (RD-017, RD-018, RD-020–RD-024)
+
+| Outcome | Class | Status in this proposal |
+|---|---|---|
+| M4 premature opening | safety (primary) | defined (§5.2); implemented |
+| M5 never protected | safety (companion), counts only | defined; implemented |
+| Missed-train rate (MTR) | safety (secondary) | defined with lead-in feasibility screen (insufficient lead-in ≠ system failure); implemented |
+| Full crossing occupancy duration | operational duration (secondary) | **DEFERRED (RD-018):** no valid same-camera pair; cross-camera alignment not approved; not reported |
+| Warning lead time, clearance latency, excess closed duration | operational / exploratory | as defined in §18; censored events excluded from point estimates |
+| Design-document metrics M1–M3, M6–M10 | — | **unimplemented / out of scope** for this proposal (non-binding reference) |
+
+Engine events are excluded from pooled M4, M5 and train aggregates (separate case study). Per-metric evaluable denominators and explicit exclusion reasons apply; no outcome-dependent global exclusion. Censored events are excluded from point estimates and counted by reason (RD-011). No combined or composite score is defined.
